#
# N1 - a checkpoint with no folded identity. Restore is identity-gated across seven
# axes and the fold is what the gate compares first, so a checkpoint without it cannot
# be gated at all. MUST trip logic:CheckpointCarriesFoldedIdentityConstraint and nothing
# else. NOT logic:CheckpointRestoreIdentityConstraint: that law COMPARES a restore's fold
# with its checkpoint's and its guard binds both, so a checkpoint carrying none falls
# outside it. The mismatch is checkpoint-restored-under-a-drifted-fold.ttl.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/logic/tests/> .

ex:ckptNoIdentity a logic:EnactmentCheckpoint ;
    rdfs:label "a checkpoint carrying no folded identity"@en .
